**1. File created:** `src/new_grep/new_grep.c`

**2. Program behavior implemented:**
- Fixed-string (byte-substring) pattern matching — not regex
- Empty pattern matches every line
- Case-sensitive matching
- Reads from stdin when no file operands; reads from files when given
- `--` terminator allows dash-prefixed patterns
- `-` is a filename operand, not a stdin alias
- Any other `-X` / `--long` argument is rejected as unknown option
- Filename prefix (`name:`) emitted only when 2+ file operands are given
- Byte-transparent: NUL bytes, invalid UTF-8, CR all treated as ordinary data
- Dynamic line buffer (no fixed-size limit)
- Per-operand error reporting (missing file, unreadable file, directory) with continuation

**3. Exit-status rules:**
- `0` — at least one line matched, no errors
- `1` — no lines matched, no errors
- `2` — any error occurred (unknown option, missing pattern, file I/O error, write error, allocation failure), regardless of whether matches were also found

